<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Menzies</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1894">1894</a>–<a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Robert Menzies was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s longest-serving prime minister, in office from 1939 to 1941 and from 1949 to 1966. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a> in 1944. His post-war government presided over a long economic boom and large-scale immigration from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anzus">ANZUS</a> treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, and expanded universities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-menzies.jpg" alt="Robert Menzies" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Library of Australia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_Menzies_1950s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
